# ==================================================================
#  .gitignore
#  OWNER: Person 6 — Lobby UI & infrastructure
# ==================================================================
#
#  WHAT THIS FILE IS
#  -----------------
#  A list of files/folders Git should NEVER track or upload.
#  One pattern per line. Lines starting with # are comments.
#  A pattern ending in / means "this folder, wherever it appears".
#
#  ⚠ DO THIS ON DAY 1, BEFORE THE FIRST `git add .`
#  If node_modules gets committed, the repo becomes huge and every PR
#  shows thousands of changed files.
#
#  PATTERNS TO ADD
#  ---------------
#  1. node_modules folder        — installed packages, rebuilt by npm install
#  2. build and dist folders     — the frontend's production output
#  3. .env and .env.* files      — secrets/config (never upload secrets)
#  4. npm debug log files        — e.g. npm-debug.log*
#  5. .DS_Store                  — macOS junk files
#  6. editor folders             — e.g. .vscode/ (optional, team choice)
#  7. Personal notes             — anything like MY_NOTES.md you don't
#                                  want the team to see
#
#  DO NOT ignore package-lock.json — CI needs it.
#
#  HOW TO CHECK IT WORKS
#  ---------------------
#  Run `git status` after `npm install`: node_modules must NOT appear.
